  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV&amp;AIDS project Central Equatoria - SSOPO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 3 year project aiming at increasing personal and community risk perceptions to reduce and prevent new HIV infections as well as re-infections most especially among the most at risk populations (i.e. youths, women, OVCs, etc) in Juba County. The project will target 205 youths/teenagers, 105 elderly people and 105 PLWHAs by equipping them with Education For Life skills to enable them reach out to their peers. Another estimated 5,000 most at risk populations and general community will be reached through drama awareness, radio and TV talk shows and out reach activities by PLWHAs. The project will also benefit 1000 PLWHAs with IGA skills, 250 bed-ridden PLWHAs with provision of home based care kits and a VCT centre to promote positive living among the PLWHAs. Another 200 OVCs will receive educational support, and 30 shelters constructed out of local materials for the elderly caring for PLWHAs in need of shelter.</narrative>
  </description>
